<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png">
  <title>How Maal uses AI | Maal</title>
  <meta name="description" content="What Maal's AI does, which providers power it, its limits, and how your data is and isn't used to improve it.">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,400..800&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/theme.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/retro-theme.css">
  <style>
    body { background: var(--bg); min-height: 100vh; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
    main { flex: 1; }
    .at-hero { padding: 5rem 1.5rem 2rem; text-align: center; }
    .at-kicker { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .18em; color: var(--fg-muted); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .at-h1 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem,6vw,3.5rem); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.03em; line-height: 1.05; }
    .at-sub { margin: 1.25rem auto 0; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--fg-muted); max-width: 600px; line-height: 1.7; }
    .at-body { max-width: 760px; margin: 2.5rem auto 4rem; padding: 0 1.5rem; }
    .at-body h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.02em; margin: 2.5rem 0 .75rem; }
    .at-body p, .at-body li { font-size: 15px; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.75; }
    .at-body ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; margin: .5rem 0; }
    .at-body li { margin: .35rem 0; }
    .at-body strong { color: var(--fg); }
    .at-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: .75rem 0; font-size: 14px; }
    .at-table th, .at-table td { text-align: left; padding: .7rem .6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); vertical-align: top; color: var(--fg-muted); }
    .at-table th { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 600; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; }
    .at-note { border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--surface); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1rem 1.2rem; margin: 1rem 0; }
    .disclaimer-block { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.5rem 4rem; font-size: 11px; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.8; }
    @media (max-width: 600px) { .at-table { font-size: 13px; } }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('partials/navbar') %>

  <main>
    <section class="at-hero">
      <p class="at-kicker">AI transparency</p>
      <h1 class="at-h1">How Maal uses AI.</h1>
      <p class="at-sub">When you use Maal you are working with an AI system, not a human financial adviser. Here is what it does, what powers it, where it falls short, and how your data is, and isn't, used to improve it.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="at-body">
      <h2>What the AI does</h2>
      <table class="at-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>How it works</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Ask Maal</strong></td><td>A large language model writes answers using your Maal data (accounts, goals, transactions, profile), your conversation, and Maal's Australian tax and super figures.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Research</strong></td><td>A multi-step pipeline gathers market data and sources, runs calculations, then writes a cited report. A second model checks the figures before you see it.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Radar</strong></td><td>Checks the conditions you set on a schedule and alerts you when one is met.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Maal Score, tax and super figures</strong></td><td>Deterministic calculations in code, tested against fixed examples, not generated by AI. Rates and thresholds come from a reviewed table that is updated each financial year.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Categories and summaries</strong></td><td>Rules plus AI classification. Your corrections take priority.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Who provides the AI</h2>
      <p>Maal sends the minimum needed to answer your request to these providers:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Anthropic</strong> (Claude): checks answers for maths and accuracy.</li>
        <li><strong>Microsoft Azure OpenAI</strong>: writes answers and reports.</li>
        <li><strong>Groq</strong>: short tasks such as titles and summaries.</li>
        <li><strong>Isaacus</strong>: pulls the relevant passage out of a document in your Vault when you ask a legal or tax question about it.</li>
        <li><strong>Exa, Finnhub and Financial Datasets</strong>: web and market information. They receive search queries and ticker symbols, not your account or contact details.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Which provider handles which task can change as Maal improves. We update this page when it does.</p>

      <h2>Limits you should know</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>AI can be wrong, out of date, or miss context. Check anything important before acting on it.</li>
        <li>Answers are only as complete as the data you have added. Maal tells you when it has too little to go on.</li>
        <li>Maal does not make decisions for you. It doesn't move money, place trades, assess credit, or approve or deny any financial product.</li>
        <li>No human reviews each answer before you see it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How your data helps Maal improve</h2>
      <div class="at-note">
        <p><strong>Your choice.</strong> Maal may use <strong>de-identified</strong> data from your chats, uploaded files and details you enter, along with usage signals (such as how many steps a question needed), to train, evaluate and improve its AI. This is on by default for new accounts and you can turn it off anytime in <strong>Settings › Privacy &amp; Security</strong>. Turning it off doesn't change the answers you get.</p>
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>De-identified first.</strong> Names, emails, account numbers, BSBs and addresses are removed or replaced before anything is used, and nothing is kept linked to your account.</li>
        <li><strong>Only from when you agreed.</strong> Data from before you saw this notice is never used, and turning the setting off removes your data from anything we build afterwards.</li>
        <li><strong>Bank data is different.</strong> Data that comes from your bank through the Consumer Data Right (via Basiq) is <strong>not</strong> used for this unless you give separate, explicit consent when you connect your bank. Maal does not ask for that consent today.</li>
        <li><strong>Never sold.</strong> Your data is not sold or used for advertising.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@hellomaal.com">hello@hellomaal.com</a>. See also our <a href="/security">security page</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="disclaimer-block">
      DISCLAIMER: Maal does not provide financial advice. Any information provided by Maal is for educational purposes only. You should do your own research. Investing is risky and you can lose all of your money.
    </div>
  </main>

  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
  <%- analyticsSnippet %>
</body>
</html>
